{{taxify_delivery_pricing}} is used inside {{delivery-pricing-courier}} service: provide courier earning proposals (before a courier accepts an order) and courier earning final calculations (after an order is delivered).


This service does not impact eater applications in any way. 


In the case of timeouts:

* On Proposal side, the timeout for createProposal endpoint is 4000 ms (quite relaxed);
** There is a try-catch on the caller side (delivery-order) and, even if the caller does not receive an answer in due time (with the proposed earnings), the courier still receives the order;
* On final courier earnings calculation – there is no timeout on the caller side (from what I saw in code):
** This call is done inside a cron job; 
** In the case of error the request is retried on the next cron run (If i read the code inside delivery-order ProcessorCron correctly);



Conclusion:

* It should not impact the business (eaters); 
* Couriers will still receive their orders and earnings;


