All problems can be summarised in the same way:*GIVEN* an initial batch (with one or multiple orders) for a specific courier;*WHEN* the batch is *NOT auto-accepted;*
*THEN* we have a "Proposal" Request;

* The request for proposal comes from {{delivery-courier-app}}

*WHEN* the batch *is auto-accepted:*
*THEN* we DO NOT have a "Proposal" Request

* Possible solution: {{delivery-courier-app}} {{delivery-order-courier}} to do a "Proposal" Request for auto-accepted batch;

*WHEN* there is a change in allocated orders for an existing batch (added or removed)
*THEN* we DO NOT have a "Proposal" Request for the new count of orders in the batch;

* Possible solution: trigger a "Proposal" Request for every change detected in existing batches ({{delivery-courier-app}} / {{delivery-order-courier}} );
* At the moment we don't have any triggers to understand when a batch is changed;

The above solutions would solve our issues:

* Any courier will have visibility over the amount of "promised" earnings, every time a batch is created or changed (*not discussing at the moment how / if the information is rendered in the Courier app)*;
* Bolt will have visibility over the amount of earnings "promised" to the courier;

