Article 27. *Advertisement of alcoholic beverages* 

27.1. The following are prohibited in the advertising of alcoholic beverages:

27.1.1. forming an opinion that as a result of using alcoholic beverages, a person will gain public reputation, achieve personal success in the profession, sports or other fields, and improve his physical or emotional condition;

27.1.2. discrediting those who do not use alcoholic beverages;

27.1.3. formation of the opinion that the use of alcoholic beverages is harmless or has beneficial, therapeutic properties for human health;

27.1.4. as the degree of darkness increases, creating an idea that the quality of alcoholic beverages will increase, presenting them as a means of quenching thirst;

27.1.5. appeal to minors regarding the use of alcoholic beverages;

27.1.6. interruption of children's and religious programs -(broadcasts)- with advertising of alcoholic beverages; [+^*[30]*^+|https://e-qanun.az/framework/30348#_edn30]

27.1.7. using images of well-known people, heroes of cinema and animation films, animals;

27.1.8. demonstration of the process of using alcoholic beverages;

27.1.9. Broadcasting of advertising of alcoholic beverages with a concentration of more than 5 percent _in television and radio programs_ from 7:00 a.m. to 11:00 p.m. [+^*[31]*^+|https://e-qanun.az/framework/30348#_edn31]

27.2. Advertising of alcoholic beverages may not be placed on the following advertising carriers:

27.2.1. alcoholic beverages with an alcohol content of more than 5 percent on the front and back covers of periodicals, on the front page of Internet information resources;

27.2.2. in printed publications, audio and video materials intended for minors;

27.2.3. in telecommunications facilities (alcohol drinks with an alcohol concentration above 5 percent);

27.2.4. advertising campaigns accompanied by the distribution and tasting of samples of alcoholic beverages are allowed only at their retail outlets, tasting halls of specialized exhibitions. Free distribution of alcoholic beverages to minors and offering samples of alcoholic beverages for tasting are prohibited in this advertising campaign.

27.3. Advertising of alcoholic beverages with an alcohol content of more than 5 percent must be accompanied by a warning that excessive consumption is harmful to health. This warning should occupy not less than 10 percent of the advertising space.

27.4. Placing advertising of alcoholic beverages on vehicles, as well as on and inside the buildings and facilities that ensure their operation (with the exception of places where the retail sale of alcoholic beverages is carried out) is prohibited.

